[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":55},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":20,"_21":22,"_23":24,"_25":-7,"_26":27},"tipo","etapa","cubo",{"_11":53,"_13":53,"_38":54},"id","guimond-separacao","nome","Separation","rascunho",false,"html","<p>After orientation, the top and bottom faces hold only white and yellow, mixed. Now the two colors go to their place: <strong>all the yellow on top and all the white on the bottom</strong>. The algorithms only use <code>R2</code>, <code>F2</code>, <code>U</code> and <code>D</code>: turns that swap corners between layers without twisting any.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R2 U' R2&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;wy&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/610efc5fa4a5fe39.svg\" alt=\"On top: one white among the yellow.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>On top: one white among the yellow.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R2 U' R2&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;wy&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/3e4f49ee621bc2e2.svg\" alt=\"On the bottom (the cube tilted): one yellow among the white.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>On the bottom (the cube tilted): one yellow among the white.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<h2>Count the whites on top</h2>\n<p>However many whites are on top, that many yellows are on the bottom: the numbers always match.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>None:</strong> done, go to <a href=\"/en/glossary#pbl\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"On the 2x2 (Ortega): puts the pieces of both layers in place at once.\">PBL</a>. (If all 4 whites are on top, also done: turn the cube over, <code>x2</code>.)</li>\n<li><strong>One or three:</strong> the <em>One and one</em> and <em>Three and three</em> cases.</li>\n<li><strong>Two:</strong> see whether the two are side by side (adjacent) or diagonal, on top and on the bottom. That&#39;s 4 cases.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Line up with U and D, do the algorithm</h2>\n<p>Turn <code>U</code> and <code>D</code> until both faces look like the case picture and do the algorithm. The most common case takes a single turn:</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama tira\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R2&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;R2&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;wy&quot;}\"><ol aria-label=\"R2\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/32dce896a90716b7-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>R2</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/32dce896a90716b7-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>Adjacent and adjacent: the top whites and the bottom yellows on the right. <code>R2</code> swaps both at once.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama tira\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R2 U' R2&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;R2 U R2&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;wy&quot;}\"><ol aria-label=\"R2 U R2\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/cdf94eaa61c9b63a-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>R2</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/cdf94eaa61c9b63a-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>U</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/cdf94eaa61c9b63a-2.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>R2</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/cdf94eaa61c9b63a-3.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>One and one: <code>R2 U R2</code>.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<p>The 6 cases, each with its top and bottom picture, are in <a href=\"/en/2x2/guimond-separacao\">Guimond Separation</a>. In the case pictures, the bottom face is drawn under the top one, seen from above, as if the cube were transparent: the front is the lower edge of each square.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> with practice, you can predict separation during <a href=\"/en/glossary#inspecao\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"The 15 seconds to look at the cube before you start solving, without turning the faces.\">inspection</a>, by working out where each corner ends up after orientation, and do both algorithms without stopping in between.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","treino","/2x2/treino?grupo=guimond-separacao","metodos",[48],"anterior",{"_13":46,"_38":47},"proximo","grupos",[28],{"_11":29,"_13":30,"_31":32,"_33":34,"_35":16,"_36":37,"_38":39},"Guimond Separação","Guimond Separation","nivel","intermediario","casos",6,"conjunto","ids",[40,41,42,43,44,45],"endereco","/2x2/guimond-separacao","2X2-GS-Vizinhos-e-vizinhos","2X2-GS-Um-e-um","2X2-GS-Tres-e-tres","2X2-GS-Diagonal-e-diagonal","2X2-GS-Diagonal-em-cima","2X2-GS-Diagonal-embaixo","Orientation","/2x2/guimond/orientacao",{"_13":49,"_50":51,"_38":52},"Guimond","numero",3,"/2x2/guimond#separacao","2x2","/2x2/",{"_56":57,"_58":59},"cubos",[62,63,64,65,66,67],"idiomas",[60,61],"pt","en",{"_11":74,"_13":74},{"_11":53,"_13":53},{"_11":73,"_13":73},{"_11":72,"_13":72},{"_11":70,"_13":71},{"_11":68,"_13":69},"pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","3x3"]
